# Fleet Console versioning

Fleet Console shows a SemVer footer (`Fleet Console vX.Y.Z`) from
`src/fleet_console/web/package.json` → Vite `__APP_VERSION__`.

This is **product UI version**, separate from fleet **Release `#N (sha)`**
(deployable robot images).

## When to bump

Bump `src/fleet_console/web/package.json` `version` (and keep
`package-lock.json` in sync) whenever you ship an **operator-visible** change:

| Change | Bump |
|--------|------|
| New screen/feature, new columns, new API fields shown in UI | **minor** (`0.1.0` → `0.2.0`) |
| Bug fix / polish that operators can notice | **patch** (`0.1.0` → `0.1.1`) |
| Breaking console UX / auth / data model reset | **major** |

Do **not** bump for pure refactors, comments, or internal-only changes with no
UI/API surface change.

## How

1. Edit `"version"` in `src/fleet_console/web/package.json`.
2. Update the top-level `"version"` fields in `package-lock.json` (or run
   `npm install` in `web/`).
3. Footer picks it up automatically via `vite.config.ts` `define`.

## After bump

Jetson hosts the console — commit + redeploy per `jetson-auto-deploy`
(`bash scripts/deploy_jetson_fleet_console.sh`, or `LOCAL_SYNC=1` when needed).
